  body: |
    # EUSS pre-settled status and the source’s qualifying-right question

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source identifies EUSS pre-settled status as limited leave and says it does not automatically establish the relevant qualifying right for the listed benefits.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 073492 explicitly refers to Memos 01/21, 01-22 and 14/25. Their effect and later case law are unresolved here. This records a bounded source statement and must not be converted into a current categorical refusal rule. The same captured part then presents an AT destitution assessment at DMG 073496–073499 (Memo 15-25): PDF page 117 uses UC wording, while its continuation and Example 1 on page 118 concern SPC. This is an explicit unresolved qualification and cross-benefit wording issue within the acquired source, not a resolved legal mapping. The judgment, Withdrawal Agreement scope, dated exclusions and memo require reconciliation before any refusal inference.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 073490, PDF page 115](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ce392fbed91051df63a90f/dmg-ch-07-part-03.pdf#page=115)
    - [DMG 073492, PDF page 115](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ce392fbed91051df63a90f/dmg-ch-07-part-03.pdf#page=115)

    - [DMG 073496–073499, AT assessment and Memo 15-25, PDF page 117](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ce392fbed91051df63a90f/dmg-ch-07-part-03.pdf#page=117)
    - [Continuation and SPC Example 1, PDF page 118](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ce392fbed91051df63a90f/dmg-ch-07-part-03.pdf#page=118)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is a model-assisted, unreviewed interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP source. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. No specialist acceptance, current-law reconciliation or complete coverage of this chapter part is claimed. References to EU law, countries and benefits retain the scope and date context of the cited text; they do not establish applicability to a person or a later regime. Machine extraction may alter reading order and characters; no visual PDF review is claimed.

