    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The memo-qualified source statement requires a further qualifying-right question for pre-settled status; later applicability is unresolved.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol2-ch7-part3/0115
      quote: "073492 [See Memo DMG 01/21][See Memo DMG 01-22][See Memo DMG 14/25] Where a claimant\nhas been granted LLR i.e. pre-settled status under the EUSS, they will not automatically have a right to\nreside which is relevant for the purposes of claiming IS, JSA, ESA or SPC. The claimant is still required to\ndemonstrate that they are exercising a qualifying right to reside under the Imm (EEA) Regs 2016, such as\nworker status, self-employed status or permanent residence."
      locator: DMG 073492
